  "kind": "budgets",
  "description": "The limits @cosyte/dicom holds its build to, judged by cosyte-bench gate in the Budgets workflow on every pull request. Peak: 20 times one input for a dense shape (the worklist item and the SR), 3 times for the CT shapes, whose bytes are almost all Pixel Data; a case still over its multiple has no peak limit and is listed with its gap in AGENTS.md, under Benchmarks. Allocation: 1.25 times the highest of the floor's 21 readings, rounded up to three significant figures. The readings of one case fall on two levels about 3.4% apart, set by the code V8's background optimizing compiler produced in that process, so a limit at the floor's own spread failed unchanged code; with this room a real allocation regression under about 25% passes the budget, and AGENTS.md says which check sees a smaller one. Throughput: the first floor's limits (its highest A/A reading plus three spreads), rounded down to two significant figures; at a benchmark's largest size it is also held to half its smallest size's slowest A/A reading. serializeDicom: CT at a single frame and at 20 frames has no throughput limit: a reading of the floor's set skipped its throughput (warmup-unstable), and a limit there would fail every reading that skips it. Import: a median cold import of at most 15 ms, which the slowest runners still miss (AGENTS.md gives the gap), and the first floor's gzipped bytes rounded up to two significant figures.",
